  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>J. C. Alexander, plumber, is listed at No. 7 <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref> in 1900. In 1905 and 1910 he is a sanitary plumber at No. 67.</p>
        <p>A Mrs C. Alexander is listed at No. 181 in 1915. That listing is not linked to this entry.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>On the electoral roll</head>
        <p>John Calder Alexander, sanitary plumber, is on the 1905 <ref target="civic?id=Electoral-Rolls">electoral roll</ref> at 67 Madeline Street.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>At No. 67, Mrs M. Dynon, grocer, is at No. 65 in 1905, and A. Heale's oyster saloon in 1910. <ref target="civic?id=Lazarus%20Cruchek">Lazarus Cruchek</ref>, furniture dealer, is two doors along at No. 71.</p>
      </div>
